WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.950
Farmers have bred cows
that give more milk,

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.010
generation after generation,

3
00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:08.250
simply by choosing
which animals to breed.

4
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.150
Scientists have made bacteria
produce human insulin,

5
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.170
by giving them one human gene.

6
00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:17.470
Two very different ways
to change living things.

7
00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:20.090
So what is really
different about them?

8
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.150
In this mission, you'll see
how selective breeding works:

9
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.810
choose parents with a
useful feature, breed them,

10
00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.140
and repeat over many generations.

11
00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:33.070
You'll find out how genetic
engineering moves a gene from one

12
00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:34.850
organism into another.

13
00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:38.850
And you'll see how bacteria
came to make insulin.

14
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:43.140
Your mission: compare two ways
of changing living things.
